hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10396","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Yazid, he said: Khaled bin Yazid told me, that He heard Abu Al-Zubayr Al-Makki speaking, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered some of his family and he was in pain. He had a fever, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is she Umm Muldam?” A woman said: Yes, so God cursed her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not curse her, for she washes away, or removes, the sins of the children of Adam just as furnace removes the impurities from iron.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10397","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Israel, he said: I heard Ja`dah, a man from Banu... Jashm bin Muawiyah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought him a man, and they said: This man wanted to kill the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You were not terrified. You were not terrified. If you had wanted that, God would not have made you do it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10398","Abu Salih Muhammad bin Zanbour al-Makki told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He has the most beautiful face, the most courageous of people, and the bravest of people in his heart. The people of Medina were terrified at night, so he went out and rode. A horse belonging to Abu Talha, naked, and he said: “You did not take care of it. You did not take care of it. Indeed, I found it in the sea.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10399","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ja’far bin Khalid bin told me Sarah, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told me, he said: Qutham and Ubayd Allah and I were playing, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He greeted him and said: “Carry this.” Then he said: “Carry this.” So Qutham carried behind him and was not ashamed of his uncle Abbas. Ubaidullah loved To Al-Abbas from Qutham, and he wiped his head three times and said: “O God, succeed Ja`far in his son.” I said: What did Qutham do? He said: He was martyred. I said: God and His Messenger know best what is good. He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10400","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Omar bin Saad, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do you not marvel that when good befalls a believer, he praises God and gives thanks, and when good befalls him Praise be to God and be patient. The believer is rewarded for everything, even the food he raises to his mouth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10401","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him. He passed by a grave in which there was a woman crying, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Fear God and be patient.” She said: And you? She did not care about my calamity. When he passed it, she was told: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the likeness of death took her, so she came to him. There is no gatekeeper besides Him. She said: O Messenger of God, for I am patient. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Patience at the first shock.”"
"10402","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: A brother told me, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When you attend the sick person, say goodness, for the angels believe.” When Abu Salamah died I said: O Messenger of God, what should I say? He said: “Say: O God, forgive us and him, and give me a good deed after him,” so he followed it from him, Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10403","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad bin Kathir al-Harrani informed us, saying: Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Tell us Thabit, he said: Omar bin Abi Salamah told me, on the authority of his mother, Umm Salamah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If If a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. O God, I consider my calamity to be with You, so reward me for it and reward me “It is better than that.” Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: he told me Ibn Umar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10404","Amr bin Mansour dictated to me, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Ibn Umar bin Abi Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: Abu Salama narrated to us, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “If a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. O God, with You I seek my calamity, so reward me for it. And give me in exchange for it something better than it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10405","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ja’far bin Khalid bin Sarah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Ja`far said: If you saw me, Qutham, and Ubayd Allah ibn al-Abbas, and we were boys playing when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by. He greeted an animal, and said: “Raise this to me.” So he put me in front of him, and said: “Raise this to Qatham,” so he placed it behind him, and he was not ashamed to His uncle, Al-Abbas, and Ubayd Allah was dearer to him than Qatham. He said: Then he wiped my head three times, then said: “O God, replace Ja’far with his family.” He said: I said: What did Qutham do? He said: He was martyred. I said: God and His Messenger know best what is good. He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10406","Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman. On the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite Yasin over your dead.”"
"10407","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to the heart of the Qur’an. A man who desires God and the Hereafter does not recite it except that he will be forgiven. Recite it on \"Your dead\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10408","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Yahya bin Abi Sulaym told me, he said: I heard Al-Jalas, he said: Marwan asked Abu Hurairah: How did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying at the funeral? He said: “O God, You created her, You guided her, You took her soul, You know her secrets and her openness. We have come as intercessors, so forgive her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10409","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of the sitting, he said: I heard Uthman bin Shammas, Marwan said. : O Abu Hurairah, how did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray at the funeral? He said: He says: “O God, You created her, and guided her to Islam, and You took her soul, and You know her secret and her revelation, we have come intercessors, so forgive her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10410","Muawiyah bin Saleh told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, he said: Abu al-Jalas told us Uqba bin Sayyar, on the authority of Ali bin Shamakh, said: I witnessed Marwan. He asked Abu Hurairah: How did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying? At the funeral? He said: He said: “O God, You are its Lord, You created it, You guided it to Islam, and You know best its secret and its revelation. We have come to intercessors, so forgive her.”"
"10411","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, on the authority of Omar bin Yunus, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Abu Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: I asked Aisha: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on The dead? She said: He used to say: “O God, forgive our living and our dead, our young and our old, our males and our females, our absent ones and our witnesses, O God, whoever of us You make alive, let him live in Islam, and whoever of us You take to death, let him die in faith.”"
"10412","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to say during prayer: “O God, forgive our living and our dead, and remember us And our two females, and our young and our old, and those who are absent and those who are present, O God, whoever of us You revive, revive him as a Muslim, and whoever You cause to die From us, cause him to die as a Muslim. O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not test us after him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10413","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of my father Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed at a funeral, he would say: “O God, forgive our living and our dead. And our young and our old, our male and our female, our witnesses and our absent ones, O God, whoever of us you revive, revive him for faith, and whoever If you take him from us, then cause him to die as a Muslim. Do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him.” Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Peace, he said: It was said about the funeral prayer, so he mentioned something like it, and said: “Whoever among us you revive, revive him as a Muslim, and whoever you cause to die From Us, so He caused him to die in the faith.” He did not mention what came after that. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: May the blessings of God be upon The dead person is to say: He mentioned something similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10414","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili told me, he said: Al-Mu’affa told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim, a man from Banu Abd al-Ashhal, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in the funeral prayer: “ O God, forgive our living and our dead, our absent and our witnesses, our males and our females, our young and our old, O God, whomever You have made alive. From us, let him live in Islam, and whoever of us you take to death, let him live in faith.” Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim. Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in prayer for the dead, something similar to his saying: “And our eldest.” He did not mention what came after that. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying over a dead person, and he heard him say something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10415","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Abu Hamza ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, peace and blessings be upon him. funeral, and he said: “O God, forgive him and have mercy on him, pardon him and keep him well, honor his place, widen his entrance, and wash him with water and ice.” And coolness, and purify it of sins as a white garment is purified of filth, and replace it with a home better than its home, and a family better than its family. And a better husband than his own, and protect him from the temptation of the grave and the torment of the Fire.”"
"10416","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Sa`id bin Amir told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “When you place your dead in the grave, say: In the name of God and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He stopped short (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10417","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah bin al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar. When the dead person was placed in the grave, he used to say: “In the name of God, and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"10418","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, complete the migration of my companions and do not return them to their heels,” but the wretched Sa’d bin Khawla, whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sympathizes with if he died in Mecca. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10419","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Harami bin Amara told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Murthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come to the graves, he would say: “Peace be upon you, the people of the house are among the believers.” And the Muslims, and we, God willing, will join you. You are our successor, and we are your successor. I ask God for well-being for us and for you.”"
"10420","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, and he is Ibn Ja`far, he said: Sharik told us, and he is Ibn Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, On the authority of Ata’, who is Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whenever it was her night. May God bless him and grant him peace. He goes out at the end of the night to Al-Baqi’ and says: “Peace be upon you, the home of a believing people, and we will meet with you tomorrow.” We are entrusted with you, and we, God willing, will join you. O God, forgive the people of Baqi’ al-Gharqad.”"
"10421","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Musa ibn Sarjis, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he was dying, and he had a cup of water in it, putting his hand into the cup and wiping it. His face with water, then he says: “Oh God, help me in the throes of death.”"
"10422","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Waki` narrated to me, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I used to hear that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not die until he has a choice between this world and the hereafter. Then hoarseness seized him during his illness in which he died, and I heard him say: With those whom God has bestowed upon among the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs. And the righteous, and those are good companions, so I thought that it was good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10423","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying upon his death: “O God, forgive me and have mercy on me, and join me with the highest companion.”"
"10424","Bishr ibn Khalid told us, he said: Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha: that When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill and died, he said: “O God, forgive me, and make me a companion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10425","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Al-Faryabi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, On the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fainted while he was on my lap, so I started to wipe him and pray for his recovery. Then he woke up and said: “Rather, I ask God for the Most High Companion, so that I may be happy with Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, peace be upon them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10426","Yahya bin Musa Khat al-Balkhi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab saying to Talha ibn Ubayd Allah: Why do I see you so disheveled or so shabby since the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died? May God bless him and grant him peace. Perhaps your only claim, O Talha, is the leadership of your cousin? He said: God forbid that I should not do that, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I know a word that he does not say.” If a man is approached by death, he finds his soul has a soul when it leaves his body, and it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.” I did not ask the Messenger May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he did not tell me about it, so he is the one who brought me in. Omar said: I know it. He said: Praise be to God, so what? She? He said: It is what he said to his uncle: “There is no god but Allah.” Talha said: You are right."
"10427","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Talha bin Ubayd Allah, he said: Omar saw Talha was sad and said: What is the matter with you, so-and-so? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, I know of a word that no servant would say upon his death unless God relieved him of his distress.” Nothing prevented me from asking him about it except the ability to do it until he died. He said: I know it. Do you know of a word that is greater than a word? His uncle ordered it: There is no god but God. He said: It is, by God, it is."
"10428","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of his father, that Omar saw him looking gloomy, so he said: “O Abu Muhammad, why do I see you so gloomy? Perhaps you are upset about the matter of your cousin, meaning Abu Bakr?” He said: No, and praised him. On Abu Bakr, but a word I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is not said by a servant at the time of his death unless God relieves him. He was distressed and his color shone, so nothing prevented me from asking about her except the power over her until he died. Omar said: I know her. Talha said: And what She? He said: Do you know a word greater than the word he offered to his uncle upon his death? Talha said: This is it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10429","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani Al-Kufi told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of his mother Sa’di, who said: Omar passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted you and said: Why are you depressed? Have you been offended by the rule of your cousin? He said: No, but I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, I know of a word that no servant utters upon his death unless it is light.” For his letter, and that his body and soul will find a soul for it.” He was arrested and I did not ask him. He said: “I know that it is the one he meant.” His uncle, and if he knew something that could save him from it, he would have ordered it. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Amer, he said: Omar passed with Talha and saw him gloomy, like him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10430","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Anas, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Umair ibn Saad, that he said: Itban ibn Malik lost his eyesight during the reign of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he sent to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I cannot pray with you in your mosque, and I would like to You pray with me in my mosque, and I will complete your prayer. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him and they mentioned Malik ibn al-Dakhsham. They said: That is a cave. The hypocrites, or he said: the people of hypocrisy, and their refuge to which they seek refuge and their stronghold. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Isn’t it He bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes, and there is no good in his testimony. He said: “No servant will bear witness to it truthfully from his heart and die unless he is deprived of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10431","Ubaid bin Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: He mentioned the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Malik bin Al-Dakhsham, was with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they fell upon him and insulted him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Call my companions for me.” They said: O Messenger of God, this is the cave of the hypocrites and their refuge to which they seek refuge. So the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Does he not bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God?” They said: Yes, and there is no good in his testimony, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “No servant bears witness to it truthfully from his heart and then dies on that account, but God will make the Fire forbidden to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10432","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Itban bin Malik told me that he was blind, so he sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Come and plan a mosque for me, and he came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his people came but a man among them was absent, called Malik bin Al-Dakhsham. They said: O Messenger of God, he And indeed, they fell into it, and the Messenger of God said: “Does he not bear witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God?” They said: He only says it seeking refuge. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one says it truthfully except that the Fire will be forbidden to him.”"
"10433","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Al-Qanabi told me, he said: Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, On the authority of Itban bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one bears witness that there is no god but God, and that I am the Messenger of God.” Then he will enter the Fire,” or he said: “The Fire will feed him.” Anas said: I liked this hadith, so I said to my son: Write it, and he wrote it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10434","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: He told me Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’ said: Itban bin Malik told us, so I met Itban bin Malik and he told me about him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “There is no one who bears witness that there is no god but God, and fire will consume him, or fire will feed him.” Anas said: I liked this hadith. So I said to my son: Write it, and he wrote it."
"10435","Suwayd ibn Nars narrated to us, saying: 'Abd Allah — meaning Ibn al-Mubarak — narrated to us from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' informed me — he claimed that he remembered the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and remembered a gush of water from a bucket that was in their dwelling — he said: \"I heard 'Itban ibn Malik al-Ansari, one of the Banu Salim, saying: I used to lead my people, the Banu Salim, in prayer. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: Indeed, my eyesight has become impaired, and the floods come between me and the mosque of my people. I wish that you would come and pray in my house at a place I could take as a mosque. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: 'I shall do so, if Allah the Exalted wills.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, came to me the next day, and Abu Bakr was with him, after the day had grown hot. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, sought permission, and I granted it to him. He did not sit until he said: 'Where would you like me to pray in your house?' I pointed to the place where I would like him to pray. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, stood, and we lined up behind him. Then he gave the salam, and we gave the salam when he gave the salam. We detained him over a prepared khazir (a dish of meat and flour). The people of the dwelling heard of it, and they came until the house was filled. A man said: 'Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshum?' One of our men said: 'That is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger.' The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: 'Do you not say that he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah?' He said: 'As for us, we see his face and his talk directed toward the hypocrites.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, also said: 'Do you not say that he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah?' He said: 'Yes, I see, O Messenger of Allah.' The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: 'No servant shall arrive on the Day of Resurrection saying: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Countenance of Allah, except that Allah shall forbid the Fire to touch him.'\" Mahmud said: \"I narrated this to a group among whom was Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, during the military expedition in which he died alongside Yazid ibn Mu'awiya. He rejected that from me and said: 'I do not think that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ever said what you have said.' That weighed heavily upon me. I made it incumbent upon myself before Allah that if He granted me safety to return from my expedition, I would ask about it from 'Itban ibn Malik if I found him alive. I set out from Iliya with the intention of Hajj and 'Umra until I arrived in Madina. I went to the Banu Salim, and there was 'Itban ibn Malik, an old, elderly man whose eyesight had gone, and he was the imam of his people. When he finished his prayer, I came to him, gave him the salam, informed him who I was, and he narrated to me just as he had narrated to me the first time.\" Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, who said: \"I asked al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, who was one of the Banu Salim and among their nobles, regarding the hadith of Mahmud, and he confirmed it accordingly.\""
"10436","Harun bin Ishaq and Ahmad bin Saad bin Abi Maryam told us, saying: Qudama bin Muhammad told us, he said: Makhramah told us, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Harb bin Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, he said: I bear witness that Abu Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me and said to me: “Give good news to the people that whoever says: There is no god but God, alone, without any partner, will have Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10437","Ahmad bin Saad told us, he said: Qudamah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Makhramah bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Harb. Ibn Zayd Ibn Khalid, on the authority of his father: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever enters the grave without any god but God, God will save him from \"fire\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10438","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id told him, on the authority of my father Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give good news to the people that whoever says: There is no god but God, it is obligatory for him \"Paradise\""
"10439","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of al-Walid Ubayy Bishr, on the authority of Hamran ibn Aban, on the authority of Uthman ibn Affan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god Except Allah, He will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10440","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Khalid, on the authority of Abu Bishr, On the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but May God enter Paradise.” Abdullah bin Hamran disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10441","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hamran, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Bayan bin Bishr, he said: I heard Humran, saying: I heard Uthman, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but God will enter \"Paradise.\" Abu Abdul Rahman told us: The hadith of Abdullah bin Hamran is an error, and the correct hadith is a treacherous hadith."
"10442","Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of al-Ma’rur, he said: I heard Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Gabriel came to me and gave me good news that whoever of your nation dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” I said: And if he steals, And if he committed adultery? He said: “Even if he steals, even if he commits adultery.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10443","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Sahmi, who is Abdullah bin Bakr, told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told me, On the authority of Wasil Al-Ahdab, on the authority of Ma’rur ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his journey, and when he was in Some night he went away and stayed for a long time, then came to us and said: “He came to me from my Lord, and he told me that whoever dies will bear witness that there is no god but God.” He will have Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, and if he steals, he said: Yes? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10444","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Bakr told us, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, that Abu Sulayman al-Juhani told him that Abu Dharr told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The king told me that he who died He bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and for him is Paradise. I still say: Even if I even say: Even if he commits adultery, and if he steals, he says: Yes.” Brief"
"10445","Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Gabriel gave me good news that whoever of your nation dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise. I said to him: Even if he commits adultery, and even if Did he steal? He said: Even if he commits adultery, or if he steals. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10446","Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb speaking, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Gabriel gave me good tidings that whoever of your nation dies will not Whoever associates anything with God will enter Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals. He said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10447","Abdah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Ibn Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Habib bin Abi told us Thabit, Suleiman Al-Amash, and Abd Al-Aziz bin Rufi’ said: We heard Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings be upon him: “Gabriel came to me and gave me good news that whoever of my nation dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals? He said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals."
"10448","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Rabbo told us, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Wahb, and on the authority of Abd al-Aziz Ibn Rafi’, Suleiman Ibn Mihran, and Bilal, they said: We heard Zayd Ibn Wahb, he said: I heard Aba Dhar, he said: “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, tell your nation that whoever among them dies will bear witness that there is no god.” Except God. He will enter Paradise. It was said: Even if he committed adultery, even if he stole. He said: Even if he committed adultery, even if he stole. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10449","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Hammad, he said: Zaid bin Wahhab Abu told me Suleiman Al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Dhar, that he heard that it might be, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so it means, he said: “The Gabriel came to me and gave me good news that whoever of my nation dies not associating anything with God will have Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, and if he steals, he said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of God, he says, meaning Gabriel: Even if he commits adultery, and if he steals, he says: Yes. Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10450","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, Qutaibah said in his hadith, Zayd ibn Wahb told us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said to us: I did not understand him as I wanted. He said: I heard Abu al-Darda’ say: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” I said: O Messenger of God, even if he commits adultery, even if he steals? He said: “Yes, even if he commits adultery, even if he steals two or three times, even if he pleases Abu Darda’.” Issa bin Abdullah bin Malik followed him"
"10451","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Isa bin Abdullah bin Malik, On the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, And that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, sincere. He will enter Paradise. I said: Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals, O Messenger of God? He said: “Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals.” I said: “Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals,” O Messenger of God? He said: “Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals, even if he pleases Abu Darda’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10452","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O Abu Darda’, go and call out: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then it is obligatory For him is Paradise.” I said: O Messenger of God, even if he commits adultery, even if he steals? He said: “Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals,” so I repeated it three times, and he said: “Even if he commits adultery, even if he steals, even if he pleases Abu al-Darda’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10453","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told us, he said: Zayd bin Waqid told us, he said: Busr told us Ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever establishes the prayer and performs Zakat, and he died not associating anything with God. It was God’s duty to forgive him, whether he immigrated or died at birth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10454","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Muhayriz, On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God forbid the Fire for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10455","Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Muhammad Issa bin Musa told me, and others, they said: he told us Ismail bin Ubayd Allah, that Qays bin Al-Harith Al-Madhaji told him: that Ubadah bin Al-Samit said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him And peace be upon him, he says: “Whoever dies not associating anything with God, God has forbidden Hell for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10456","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Mushar told us, he said: Sadaqa bin Khaled told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid told us. Bin Jabir, he said: Umair bin Hani told me, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Ubadah bin al-Samit, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God alone, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Jesus is the servant of God and the son of his nation.” And His word which He delivered to Maryam and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true, and that Hell is true, God admitted him through any of the eight gates of Paradise. \"He willed\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10457","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Umair bin Hani, he said: Junada bin Abi Umayyah told me, On the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger And that Jesus is the servant of God and His word which He bestowed upon Mary and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and Hell is true, God admitted him into Paradise for what he was. “of work” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10458","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah, our neighbor, on the authority of Anas bin Malik The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Muadh bin Jabal: “Know that whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god but God will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10459","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Hamza told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Muadh bin Jabal: “Know that whoever bears witness that there is no god but God will enter Paradise.”"
"10460","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Muadh Ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies bears witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, with certainty of His heart has entered Paradise.” Shu’bah said: I did not ask Qatada: Did you hear it from Anas? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10461","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, he said: Anas told us, he said: And he mentioned to us The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Muadh bin Jabal: “Whoever meets God not associating anything with Him will have Paradise.” He said: Do I not give good tidings to people? He said: “They do not trust.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10462","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Hasan bin Kahil, He said: I entered the mosque and sat next to a sheikh, and he said: Muadh bin Jabal told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, he said: “There is no soul that dies that bears witness that it does not There is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God. This goes back to a heart of truthfulness, unless God forgives her.” I said: Did you hear it from Muadh bin Jabal? It was as if the people had rebuked me. He said: Do not rebuke him. I heard that from Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: To some of them: Who is this? They said: This is Abd al-Rahman bin Samra. Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Humayd bin Hilal, on the authority of Hasan bin Al-Kahen, and he was His father was a priest in pre-Islamic times"
"10463","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj al-Sawaf, he said: Humayd bin Hilal told me, he said: Hsan told me Ibn Al-Kahen Al-Adawi, he said: I sat in a gathering in which Abdul-Rahman Ibn Samurah was present, and I do not know him. He said: Muadh Ibn Jabal told us, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not a soul on earth that dies that does not associate anything with God, bearing witness that I am the Messenger of God. That person will return to his heart.” Certain that she will be forgiven.” I said: Did you hear it from Muadh? So the people rebuked me, so he said: Leave him, for he did not speak badly. Yes, I heard it from Muadh. He claimed that he heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"10464","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Muttalib bin Hantab narrated to me Al-Makhzoumi, he said: Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Amra told me, he said: My father told me, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a battle. The people were struck by starvation, so the people asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to slaughter some of their backs and said: God will inform us of it. When Omar ibn al-Khattab saw that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was about to give them permission to slaughter some of their backs, he said: Oh Messenger of God, how about us if we meet the enemy starving in men? But if you decided, O Messenger of God, to invite the people with what was left of their provisions, So she gathers them, and makes them beautiful, and then supplicates to God for blessing therein. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for their provisions, and the people made They come, meaning a small amount of food and more than that, and the highest among them was the one who brought a cup of dates, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, collected them. He greeted him, then he stood up and called for what God wished for him to call, then he called the army with their containers and ordered them to mobilize, and not a single container was left in the army. However, they filled it and what was left of it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until its roots became visible, then he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” “And I bear witness that I am the Messenger of God. No believer who is certain of them will meet God except that the Fire will be withheld from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"10465","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh told us in his hadith, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that a cyclist, Abu al-Samh He told him, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “He said: O Lord, teach me something by which I may remind You And I call upon You by Him. He said: O Moses: There is no god but God. Moses said: O Lord, all of Your servants say this. He said: Say: There is no god but God. He said: No. There is no god but You. I only want something that you can specialize in for me. He said: O Moses, if only the seven heavens and their ruler were other than Me, and the seven earths were on one hand, and there is no god. “There is no god but God.”"
"10466","I am Ismail bin Masoud, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith. Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Hafs bin Asim narrates, on the authority of Abu Saeed bin Al-Mu’alla, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by him while he was praying, and he called him. He said: So I prayed, then I came to him. He said: “What prevented you from answering me?” He said: I was praying. He said: “Did not God Almighty say: O you who have believed, respond to God and to the Messenger.” When He calls you to revive you, shall I not teach you the greatest Surah before I leave the mosque? He said: So he went to leave. I said: O Messenger? God, your saying, He said: “Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, these are the Seven Repeated Verses, and the Great Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10467","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Malik. And Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it while I was hearing from him, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated to me, and the pronunciation for it, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman said that he heard Abu Al-Sa’ib, the servant of Hisham bin Zahra, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qur’an is not recited is prematurity, it is prematurity, it is prematurity, incomplete.”"
"10468","I said: O Abu Hurairah, am I sometimes behind the imam? He touched my arm and said: Recite it, O Persian, to yourself, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God Almighty said: God Almighty: I divided the prayer between Me and My servant into two halves: half of it is for Me, and half of it is for My servant, and My servant is entitled to whatever he asks.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. And peace be upon him: “Recite. The servant says: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. God Blessed and Most High says: My servant has praised me. The servant says: The Most Gracious. The Most Merciful. God says: My servant has praised me. The servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment. God says: My servant has glorified me. The servant says: You are we to worship? And to You we seek help. This verse is between Me and My servant, and My servant has what he asks. The servant says: Guide us to the straight path {6} The path of those I have bestowed upon them neither those with wrath nor those who go astray. {7} So these are for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks.”"
"10469","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the imam says: Neither those with anger nor those who go astray, then say: Amen, for whoever whose words agree with the words of the angels will be forgiven for what came before. \"from his sin\""
"10470","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan, narrated to me by Al-Harith bin Atiya, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believers will gather on the Day of Resurrection and say: If only we had interceded to our Lord so that He would grant us relief from... This is our place. They will come to Adam and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind. God created you with His own hand, and made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you The names of everything, so intercede for us with your Lord so that you may relieve us from this place of ours.” He cited the hadith of intercession in its entirety."
"10471","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Protest Adam and Moses, peace be upon them, and Moses said to him: O Adam, God created you with His hand, then He breathed into you of His Spirit, then He said to you: Be, and you were. He commanded the angels and they prostrated to you, then he said: Reside in Paradise, you and your wife, and eat from it freely wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree. So you will be among the wrongdoers. He forbade you from one tree, so you disobeyed your Lord. Then Adam said: O Moses, did you not know that God had decreed this for me before? To create me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Adam and Moses performed Hajj. Adam and Moses performed Hajj."
"10472","I am Issa bin Hammad, I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Adam met Moses, and Moses said to him: You are the one who did this to us. You were in Paradise, so you brought us down to The earth? Then Adam, peace be upon him, said to him: Are you Moses to whom God gave the Torah? He said: Yes. He said: How long do you find that the Torah was written before my creation? Moses, peace be upon him: With such and such. Adam said: Why did you find my sin in it? He said: Yes. He said: So do you blame me for something that God has decreed for me before? My morals? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then Adam and Moses performed Hajj. So Adam and Moses performed Hajj. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10473","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: Which sin is greater in the sight of God? He said: “That you make a rival to God while He created you.” I said: That is great. I said: Then what? He said: “Then you kill your child so that he may eat with you.” I said: Then what? He said: “To commit adultery with your neighbor’s girlfriend.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10474","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim and Ali bin Hajar. They said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Amr Ibn Harith, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Truffles are from manna.” Ali said in his hadith: What God sent down upon the Children of Israel, and its water is a cure for the eyes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10475","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammam bin Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “It was said to the Children of Israel: ‘Enter the gate, prostrating yourself and saying, ‘Hatta.’” So they entered the gate, crawling on their steps, and they moved. They said: “Wheat, a grain in a hair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10476","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, in his saying: “A piece of wheat.” He said: “They changed it,” and they said: “A grain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10477","I am Al-Hasan bin Ahmad bin Habib. Muhammad, who is the son of Abdullah bin Numayr, narrated to us, narrated to us Waki’, narrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Alqamah said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: “For those who write the book with their own hands. It was revealed about the People of the Book.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10478","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, from Khalid, meaning bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, God willing, he said: Abdullah bin Salam came to the Messenger of God He, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived at Medina and said: I am asking you about three things that only a prophet knows: What are the first signs of the Hour? And the first thing the people of Paradise will eat, and the child will go back to his father and to his mother? He said: “Gabriel, peace be upon him, told me about them just before.” Abdullah said: “That is a vile angel, an enemy of the Jews. He said: “As for The first signs of the Hour: a fire that will gather them from the east to the west, and as for the first food that the people of Paradise will eat: an increase in liver A whale, and as for the child: if it precedes the man’s fluid, it will be removed, and if it precedes the woman’s fluid, it will be removed.” He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. He said: O Messenger of God, the Jews are a people of confusion, even if they knew of my Islam before you asked them about me. They astonished me before you, and the Jews came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “Which man among you is Abdullah bin Salam?” They said: The best of us and the son of our best, our master and the son of our master, and the most knowledgeable of us. He said: “What did you think if Abdullah bin Salam converted to Islam?” They said: May God protect him. From that, he went out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Our evil and the son of our evil. And they disparaged him. He said: This is what I feared, O Messenger of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10479","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"That which befell Sulayman ibn Dawud, upon him be peace, was on account of a woman from his household called Jarada. She was the most beloved of his women to him. Whenever he wished to go to his women or enter the privy, he would give her the ring. Then some people of Jarada's family came disputing with a group before Sulayman ibn Dawud, upon him be peace. Sulayman's desire was that the truth would be in favor of Jarada's family so he could rule in their favor. But he was punished when his desire was not one with theirs. Then, when Allah willed to test him, he gave her the ring and entered the privy. The Shaytan appeared in the form of Sulayman and said: 'Give me my ring.' She gave him his ring, and he put it on. When he put it on, the Shaytins, mankind, the jinn, and everything submitted to him. Sulayman came and said: 'Give me my ring.' She said: 'Leave! You are not Sulayman.' Sulayman, upon him be peace, said: 'That is from the affair of Allah. It is a trial by which I have been tested.' He left, and whenever he said, 'I am Sulayman,' they would stone him until they bruised his heels. He went out carrying on the shore of the sea, while this Shaytan remained dwelling among them, marrying his women and judging among them. When Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, willed to restore the kingdom to Sulayman, the Shaytins set out and wrote books containing magic and disbelief, and buried them beneath the throne of Sulayman, upon him be peace. Then they unearthed them and said: 'This is what used to mislead the jinn and mankind.' The people disbelieved in Sulayman, until Allah raised Muhammad, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed upon Muhammad, upon him be peace: 'And Sulayman did not disbelieve, but the Shaytins disbelieved' — meaning what they had done. Sulayman went out carrying on the shore of the sea. When the people denied him, and when Allah willed to restore the kingdom to Sulayman, they denied him. The Shaytins went out to his women and asked them, and they said: 'Indeed, he comes to us while we are menstruating, and he did not used to come to us before that.' When the Shaytan saw that his destruction was imminent, he fled and was sent into the sea. In the hadith, a fish swallowed him and took it. The Shaytan went out until he reached an island in the sea. Sulayman, upon him be peace, went out carrying a fish for a man. He said: 'How much will you carry?' He said: 'A fish like this fish.' He carried it with him until he reached him and gave him the fish that had the ring in its belly. When he gave him the fish, he split its belly, intending to roast it, and there was the ring! He put it on, and the mankind and the Shaytins came to him. He sent in pursuit of the Shaytan, and they could not overpower him. He said: 'Find a stratagem for him.' They went and found him asleep, having become intoxicated. They built over him a house of lead. Then they came to seize him, but he leapt, and whenever he leapt in any direction, he would remove the lead with him. They seized him and brought him to Sulayman. He ordered that a marble vessel be hollowed out, placed him inside it, and sealed it with copper. Then he ordered that it be cast into the sea.\""
"10480","I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Asif was a scribe Solomon the son of David, peace be upon him, and he knew the Greatest Name. He used to write down everything that Solomon, peace be upon him, commanded him to do, and bury it under His throne, and when Solomon died, the devils cast him out, and they wrote magic, lies, and disbelief between every line, and they said: This is what he used to do. Solomon with it, but the ignorant and foolish people declared him a disbeliever and reviled him, and their scholars stood still, and their ignorant people continued reviling him, until he was revealed. God Almighty: And they followed what the devils recited about the kingdom of Solomon, and Solomon did not disbelieve, but the devils disbelieved. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10481","I am Amr bin Ali, from Yahya, from Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar said: “My father told us to read it. And Ali judged us, and we will rely on what my father said, and that is because he says: Do not abandon anything that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God Almighty has said: We do not abrogate any verse or make it forgotten, We bring back something better than it or something similar to it."
"10482","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Al-Nadr, I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, he said: I said to Saad bin Malik: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, reciting: “0 We do not abrogate a verse or make it forgotten.” He said: God did not recite the Qur’an to Al-Musayyab, nor to his son. And it is only: 0 We abrogate a verse or you forget it, O Muhammad. He said: And remember your Lord if you forget. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10483","10578 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman told me, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulayman, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Umar: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying on his camel wherever it headed, then he recited this verse: So wherever they turn Then there is the face of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10484","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, I am Humaid Al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, If you had taken the place of Abraham as a place of prayer, then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: “And take the place of Abraham as a place of prayer.”"
"10485","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you not see that when your people built the Kaaba, they deviated from the foundations of Abraham?” So I said: O Messenger of God, will you not return it to the foundations of Abraham? Abraham? He said: “If it had not been for the two incidents of disbelief among your people.” Abdullah bin Omar said: If Aisha had heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, neglecting to touch the two pillars that surround the stone, except that the house was not built according to the foundations. Abraham (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10486","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, who said: “The Messenger of God came May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed with Nahu and the Holy House for sixteen months. Then he headed to the Kaaba. Then a man passed by who was He prayed with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, over a group of Ansar, and he said: I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to the Kaaba. Then they turned to the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10487","I am Muhammad bin Hatim, I am Habban, I am Abdullah, I am a partner, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, in his saying: “The foolish people will say what And he turned them away from the direction they were following. He said: “They are the foolish People of the Book.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10488","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: While the people were standing in Quba during the morning prayer, Someone came to them and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was revealed to him tonight and he was commanded to face the Qiblah, so face it.” “And their faces were towards the Levant, so they turned to the Kaaba.”"
"10489","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naim, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace and the Holy House for sixteen months, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loved to pray with the Kaaba. So he was raising his head to the sky, and then God Almighty revealed: We have seen the turning of your face in the sky, so We will certainly turn you to a qiblah that will please you. So, “Your face is towards the Sacred Mosque.” Al-Bara’ said: And the direction towards us is the one before it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10490","And he said regarding the words of God Almighty: “That your faith should be lost.” He said: “God would not waste the prayer of one who died while praying Nahu and the Holy House.”"
"10491","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib, I am Al-Layth, we are Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, he said: He told me Marwan bin Othman, that Ubaid bin Hunayn told him, on the authority of Abu Saeed bin Al-Mu’alla, who said: “We used to go to the market in the morning during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. We passed by the mosque and prayed in it. One day we passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting on the pulpit. I said: Something happened, so I sat down and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: We may see the turning of your face in the sky, until he finished reciting the verse. I said To my companion: Let us kneel two rak’ahs before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descends, so that we will be the first to pray, so we hid ourselves and prayed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down and prayed the noon prayer for the people on that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10492","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Yahya bin Adam, we are Abu Zubaid, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas, he said: “No one remained who prayed The two qiblahs are other than me.”"
"10493","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Hisham bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, I am Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “We have made you a moderate nation.” He said: “Just.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10494","I am Muhammad bin Adam bin Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The Prophet will come on the Day of Resurrection with a man, and the Prophet will come with two men, and the Prophet will come with him more than that, and it will be said to him: Have you conveyed the message to your people? They say: Yes. Then they are called and it is said: Did you convey the message? They say: No. Then it is said: Who bears witness to you? He says: The nation of Muhammad May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, will be called and it will be said: Has this conveyed the message? They will say: Yes. It will be said: And what do you know? So they say: Our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us that the messengers had conveyed the message, so we believed him. That is what he said: And likewise. “We have made you a just nation,” he said, “justly, so that you may be witnesses over the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10495","I am Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, I am Bahz, I am Hammad bin Salamah, I am Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions were They pray near the Holy Mosque, and when this verse was revealed: So turn your face towards the Sacred Mosque, a man from Banu Salamah passed by. So he called out to them while they were kneeling in the Fajr prayer: “The qibla has been turned towards the Kaaba, so they leaned forward and bowed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10496","0 I am Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, he said: I said to Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was young at that time: Did you see what God Almighty said: “Indeed, Safa Al-Marwah is one of the rituals of God, so whoever makes the Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no sin on him if he circumambulates them. Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 158. I do not see anything wrong with anyone except He circumambulates them. Aisha said: No, if it were as she says, then it would be: There is no sin on him if he does not circumambulate them. Rather, this verse was revealed in The Ansar were making the crescent moon at Manat, and Manat was on the same path as Qudayd, and they were eager to circumambulate between Safa and Marwah. When he came Islam They asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and God Almighty revealed: Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God, so whoever performs Hajj Whether he visits the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame on him for circumambulating them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10497","I am Harun bin Abdullah, and Yusuf bin Saeed, and the word for it is, Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ismail bin Umayyah informed me, On the authority of Ayyub ibn Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took me by the hand and said: “ God created the soil on Saturday, He created the mountains on Sunday, He created the trees on Monday, He created the hated on Tuesday, and He created light. on Wednesday, and He spread the animals therein on Thursday, and He created Adam on Friday after the afternoon, the last of creation, the last hours of the day.”"
"10498","We are Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am An-Nadr bin Shumail, we are Shu`bah, I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, and Ismail bin Masoud. They said: We are Khaled. He is Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who “He who dies does not make a rival to God, He admits him to Hell.” And I say: Whoever dies, making no rival to God, He admits him to Paradise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10499","I am Al-Haytham bin Ayyub, from Yahya bin Zakaria, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever swears an oath to part with money will meet God while He is angry with him, and it is confirmed in the Book of God Almighty: Indeed, those who buy For the covenant of God and their oaths, a small price. These will have no share in the Hereafter.” He said: Then Al-Ash’ath bin Qays came and said: Abu Abd is not telling you. The Most Gracious? We said: Such and such. He said: It is true, by God. It was revealed about me and so-and-so, the son of so-and-so. There was a dispute between me and him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your witnesses.” Or his oath.” I said: Then he swears. He said: “Whoever swears an oath and swears money by it while he is lying about it will meet God while He is angry with him.” Then God Almighty revealed this verse"
"10500","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Kharsha bin Al-Harr On the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There are three whom God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them, nor will He purify them. And for them is a painful torment. Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. He said: The one who sends his burden is lost, and the one who spends is rewarded by false oaths and benevolence. \"His giving\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10501","I am Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The retaliation was in Children of Israel, but there was no blood money among them, so God, Blessed and Most High, said to this nation: Retaliation for the murdered is prescribed for you: a free for a free. To his saying: Whoever is pardoned from his brother in any way, the pardon is that the blood money is accepted intentionally, and following what is right is that you follow this. Kindly and do this with kindness, so make it easy for this nation.”"
"10502","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, narrated by Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The day of Ashura was a day on which the Quraysh fasted.” In the pre-Islamic era, the Messenger of God used to fast it, and when he came to Medina, he fasted it, and ordered that he fast it, so the fast of Ramadan was revealed, so Ramadan was The obligatory duty, whoever wishes may fast on the day of Ashura, and whoever wishes may leave it.”"
"10503","I am Qutayba bin Saeed. He said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Arak told him, that Urwa told him, on the authority of Aisha: The Quraysh used to fast on the day of Ashura in the pre-Islamic era, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to fast until Ramadan was imposed, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wants, let him fast from it, and whoever wants, let him break his fast.”"
"10504","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Bakr, meaning bin Mudar, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of Salama bin Al-Akwa’ said: “When this verse was revealed: And those who are able to bear it must make a ransom by feeding a poor person. Those of us who wanted to break the fast And he ransoms himself, until the verse after it was revealed and abrogated it.”"
"10505","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in His saying: “And those who are able to bear it must pay a ransom of feeding one poor person.” He volunteered and provided for another poor person. It is not abrogated. It is better for him, and for you to fast is better for you. This is not permitted except for an elderly person who does not able to fast, and the sick person who cannot be cured.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10506","I am Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab, we are Muhammad bin Sabiq, we are Warqa’, we are Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Those who encircle it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10507","I am Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali, narrated by Khalaf bin Tamim, on the authority of Bashir Abi Ismail, Khaythamah narrated to me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, regarding fasting in Ramadan In the book, I said: Where is this verse: “A number of other days?” He said: It was revealed on the day it was revealed, meaning upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “We journeyed hungry and disembarked not satiated, and today we journeyed sated and disembarked satiated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10508","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Shabi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about His statement: “Until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The white thread is distinct from the black thread. This black is the black of the night and the white of the day.”"
"10509","I am Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, we are Saeed bin Abi Maryam, I am Abu Ghassan, Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: “It was revealed This verse: “And eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread, and it did not descend: at dawn, and there were men If they want to fast, one of them ties a white thread and a black thread around his foot, and continues to eat and drink until it becomes clear to him. I saw them, and after that God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: “of dawn,” and they knew that he meant by that: “night and day.”"
"10510","I am Hilal bin Al-Ala, I am Husayn bin Ayyash, I am Zuhayr, I am Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Azib, “If one of them slept before To have dinner, it is not permissible for him to eat anything or drink all night and day from tomorrow until the sun sets, until this verse was revealed: And eat and drink, to: The Black Thread, and it was revealed about Abu Qais bin Amr, he came to his family while he was fasting after sunset, and he said: Is there anything? So his wife said: We have nothing, but I will go out and look for dinner for you. So she went out, and he laid down his head and fell asleep, so she came back. To him, I found him sleeping, and I woke him up and he did not eat anything, and he spent the night fasting and fasting in the morning, until the middle of the day, when he fainted, and that Before the verse was revealed, then God revealed it.”"
"10511","I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, from Umayyah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, “When the Ansar performed Hajj, they would not enter from its doors, and entered from its backs, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: And there is no righteousness that you approach houses from their backs."
"10512","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naim, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, in his saying: “And righteousness is not that Enter houses from their fronts. He said: When people of pre-Islamic times entered ihram, they did not enter houses from their doors, but entered them from Its backs are from the walls, so God Almighty revealed: And righteousness is not that you approach houses from their backs, but righteousness is he who fears and comes \"Houses from their doors\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10513","I am Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Khaled bin Abdullah, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Wabara, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr He said: Ibn Umar came out to us, and we were hoping that he would tell us a strange hadith. Then a man approached him with the question and said: O Abu Abd. The Most Gracious, what prevents you from fighting, when God Almighty says: And fight them until there is no strife? He said: Your mother has bereaved you. Do you know what temptation is? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was only fighting the polytheists, and entering into their religion was a temptation, and he was not fighting them over the kingdom.”"
"10514","I am Muhammad bin Hatim bin Naim, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Rukin bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Umaylah, on the authority of Yasir Ibn Umaylah, on the authority of Khuraym Ibn Fatik Al-Asadi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever spends an expenditure in the way of God, it will be recorded for him seven \"a hundred times\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10515","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, he said: Aslam told me. Abu Imran, he said: Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When God strengthened Islam and increased its supporters, some of us said: We have a secret between us: God Almighty has strengthened Islam and increased its supporters. If only we would take care of our wealth and make amends from it, then God Almighty would send down And glory be to Him, and this was brought back to us: And spend in the cause of God, and do not throw yourselves into destruction with your own hands, but do good. Indeed, God loves those who do good. So it was “Destruction is residing in our property.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10516","I am Muhammad ibn Hatim, I am Hibban, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Haywa, Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed me, I was informed by Aslam Abu Imran, he said: We were, and upon The people of Egypt were Uqba bin Amir, and the people of the Levant were Fadhalah bin Ubaid. Then a large column of Romans left the city, and we lined up for them. A large line of Muslims, and a man of the Muslims carried the Roman line until he entered them, then he came out to us, and the people shouted, and they said: Glory be to God, the boy threw his hand into destruction, and Abu Ayyub, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people, you You interpret this verse according to this interpretation, and this verse was only revealed about us, the Ansar, when God strengthened his religion and multiplied it. His supporters, we said to each other secretly from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Our money has been lost, so if we had stayed in it... And we repaired what was lost, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed in His Book, responding to us what we were concerned about. He said: And spend in the way of God. And do not throw yourselves into destruction, for destruction was the settlement that we wanted to establish in our property and put it right, so we were commanded. By conquest.” Abu Ayyub continued to fight in the cause of God until he was arrested. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10517","I am Amr bin Ali, from Azhar bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ajra, he said: In me This verse was revealed, so I came, and he said: “Come closer.” I approached, and he said: “Are your worries harming you?” So he ordered me to fast, or give charity, or A ritual,” Ibn Aoun said: Mujahid explained it to me but I did not memorize it, so I asked Ayoub, and he said: Fasting for three days, and giving alms for six. Poor people, and rituals as long as possible.”"
"10518","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asbahani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, he said: I sat in this The mosque went to Ka’b ibn Ujrah, so I asked him about this verse: “So a ransom for fasting.” Ka’b said: “It came down to me, and I was harmed by... My head, so I was carried to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while lice were scattered on my face. He said: “I did not see that you had exerted as much as you did.” I see, do you find a sheep?” He said: No, then this verse was revealed: It is a ransom of fasting, charity, or rituals. Fasting is for three days. The charity is given to six poor people, for each poor person half a saa’, and the ritual ritual is a sheep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10519","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, from Bishr, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Imran, who said: “The Verse of Mut’ah was revealed, meaning: Mut’at al-Hajj. In the Book of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded it. No verse was revealed that annulled the verse Mut’at al-Hajj, nor did he forbid it. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until he died. A man said: “In his opinion, whatever he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10520","I am Saeed bin Abdul Rahman. Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “And provide The best provision is piety. He said: There were people performing Hajj without provision, so it was revealed: And provide for yourself, for the best provision is piety."
"10521","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Abu Muawiyah, we are Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Quraysh were standing at Muzdalifah. They are called Al-Hums, and all the Arabs stop at Arafat, so God commanded His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to stop at Arafat, then move away from it. Then God Almighty revealed: “Then disperse from where the people disperse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10522","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, he said: Qatada asked Anas: What supplication was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace, does he pray for it more often? He said: He used to supplicate most often with this saying: “O God, give us goodness in this world and goodness in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.”"
"10523","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim. Waki’ told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The most hateful of men to God is the most bitter adversary.”"
"10524","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Sulayman bin Harb, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “When the Jews menstruated They did not eat with women, nor drink with them, nor have intercourse with them in the houses, so they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. Then God Almighty revealed: “And they ask you about menstruation. Say, ‘It is a harm.’ So keep away from women during menstruation.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded them. He granted them to eat with them, to drink with them, to have intercourse with them in the houses, and to do everything to them except sexual intercourse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10525","I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Jews used to say about a man who brings his wife from Before her anus, in her anus: That the child will be cross-eyed, so it was revealed: Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage however you wish."
"10526","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Abu Awanah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: “The Jews said: If he comes If a man has intercourse with his wife before her anus, it has been a year since that time, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage. “Whatever you like, he said: standing, sitting, and blessing, after he was in the dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10527","I am Ahmad bin Al-Khalil, we are Yunus bin Muhammad, we are Yaqoub, we are Jaafar, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar bin The letter was addressed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, I have perished. He said: What destroyed you? He said: I turned around. tonight, but nothing was answered. He said: Then God revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, this verse: Your women are your tillage. So cultivate your tillage wherever you wish. He says: “Early, and retreat, and beware of menstruation and menstruation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10528","I am Sawwar bin Abdullah bin Sawwar, we are Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, we are Abbad bin Rashid, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, saying: Maqil told me Ibn Yasar said: “I had a sister who was getting engaged, so I prevented her. Then a cousin of mine proposed to her, so I married her to him, and they were together as long as God willed.” They would be companions, then he divorced her with a divorce that he had the right to take back from her, so he left her until her waiting period was over, and the suitor proposed to her, came and proposed to her, So I said: O fool, you proposed to my sister, but the people prevented her from doing so, and I preferred you to her. I divorced her, but when her waiting period was over, you came to propose to her? No, by God, no There is no god but Him. I will not give you in marriage. This verse was revealed about me: And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from marrying you. Their wives if they agreed, so I said: “I heard and obeyed, I atone for my oath and married her.”"
"10529","I am Abu Bakr bin Ali. Suraij bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hushaym. I am Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar. He said: “I married my sister A man from among us divorced her, and when the waiting period was over, he proposed to her and she agreed to that, so I said to him: I married you and preferred you, then I divorced her. What is the matter with the one that returns to you? So it was revealed: And when you divorce women and they have reached their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when They agreed among themselves in a kind manner, so I said when this verse was revealed: “She will return to you.”"
"10530","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, I am Khalid, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, I am Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I met Malik, and I said: How was Ibn Masoud says about Subayah? He said: He said: “Do you impose a burden on her, and do not give her a concession, for Surat An-Nisa, the shorter one, was revealed after the tall one?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10531","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah, on the authority of his paternal aunt Zainab bint Ka’b bin Ajra, that Al-Furai’ah bint Malik ibn Sinan, who is the sister of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, told her: She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, asked him: Should she return to her family, Banu Khudra, for her husband went out in search of a slave of his. They stayed until they were on the outskirts of The one who came caught up with them and they killed him. She said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if I should return to my family, as my husband had not left me in A house that he owns and no expenses. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes,” so I went out until I was in the room, or in The mosque. He called me or ordered me, so I was invited. He said: “How did you say?” She said: I responded to him, and he said: “Stay in your house until the letter is conveyed.” “For him,” I waited for four months and ten days, and when Uthman sent for me, I informed him, so he followed him and decided for him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10532","On the authority of Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yusuf, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Hazm, on the authority of Humaid bin Nafi’, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, who said: I went to see Umm Habibah when her father, Abu Sufyan, died, so she called for perfume and applied it to her. A slave girl, then she touched her private parts, then said: By God, I have no need for perfume, except that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “It is not permissible for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn a dead person for more than three days, except for a period of fourteen months and ten days.”"
"10533","This is Ishaq bin Ibrahim, I am Isa, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Shutair bin Shikal, on the authority of Ali, peace be upon him, who said: They occupied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he stopped the afternoon prayer until he prayed it between the two evening prayers, and he said: “They have distracted us from the middle prayer, may God fill their homes.” And their graves will be fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10534","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik. And Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ Ibn Hakim, on the authority of Abu Yunus, the servant of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Aisha ordered me to write to her A copy of the Qur’an, and she said: If you reach this verse, then call me: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer.” When she reached her, I called her, so she hoped. Ali: “Guard the prayers, the middle prayer, and the afternoon prayer, and stand obedient to God.” Then she said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10535","I am Suwaid bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Harith, who is Ibn Shubail, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: “During the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of us was speaking to his companion during prayer regarding his need, until this verse was revealed: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer and stand obedient to God.” At that time we were commanded to remain silent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10536","I am Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad, I am Uthman bin Omar, I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ There was a woman from the Ansar who did not have a child, so she made a burden on herself. If she had a child, she would make him a Judaizer. When the Ansar embraced Islam, They said: What should we do to our children? Then this verse was revealed: There is no compulsion in religion. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10537","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, in his hadith, on the authority of bin Abi Adi, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “A woman used to impose on herself, if a child of hers lived, that she should make him a Judaizer. When Banu al-Nadir were expelled, there were among them some of the sons of the Ansar. They said: We do not leave our children, so God Almighty revealed: There is no compulsion in religion. Rightliness has become distinct from error. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10538","I am Amr bin Mansour, we are Abdullah bin Muhammad, we are Juwayriyah, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, And Abu Ubaid told him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on Abraham, we are more deserving of doubt than him. He said: My Lord, show me how You bring the dead to life. He said: Do you not believe? He said: Yes, but to reassure my heart. So he mentioned the verse, and may God have mercy on Lot, who was sheltering in A severe situation. If I had stayed in prison, Joseph would not have stayed. Then the caller came to me and I would have answered him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10539","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The The devil has a fault, and the angel has a fault. As for the devil’s fault, it is a promise of evil and a denial of the truth, but as for the angel’s fault, it is a promise of good. And believing in the truth, so whoever finds any of that, let him know that it is from God, let him praise God, and whoever finds any of the other, let him seek refuge from Satan. Then he recited: Satan promises you poverty and commands you to commit immorality, but God promises you forgiveness from Him and bounty."
"10540","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Al-Faryabi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “They hated to submit to their kinsmen among the polytheists, so they asked, and he submitted to them, and this was revealed.” Verse: It is not your responsibility to guide them, but God guides whom He wills, and whatever good you spend is for yourselves, and you do not spend except seeking the pleasure of God, and whatever good you spend is for yourselves. If you spend of good, it will be repaid to you, and you will not be wronged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10541","I am Ali Ibn Hajar, I am Ismail, I am a partner, on the authority of Ata Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not the poor person who is rejected by one date and two dates, and a bite and two mouthfuls. Rather, it is the poor person who is chaste. Read if you like: They do not ask. \"people are stubborn\""
"10542","I am Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Al-Mu’tamir. He is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to Alqamah: He said: Abdullah: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the one who consumes usury, the one who pays it, the two witnesses to it, and the one who writes it down”? He said: The one who consumes usury, and the one who pays it. I said: And the two witnesses to it, and the one who writes it down? He said: We only narrate what we heard (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10543","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, I am Abu Dawud, I am Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-A'mash. And I am Bishr bin Khalid, I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “When The last verses of Surat Al-Baqarah were revealed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the mosque, recited them in the mosque, and declared it forbidden. “Trading in wine,” the wording is by Mahmoud"
"10544","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, from Waki’, from Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha: “When the verses of usury were revealed, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the pulpit, recited them to the people, then forbade trading in wine."
"10545","I am Al-Hussein bin Harith, I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Another Something revealed from the Qur’an: “And fear a day in which you will be returned to God.”"
"10546","I am Muhammad bin Aqeel, I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, my father told me, Yazid told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “And fear A day in which you will be returned to God. Then every soul will be paid in full what it has earned, and they will not be wronged. It is the last verse that was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. \"And he greeted\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10547","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, I am Waki’ na Sufyan, on the authority of Adam bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When this was revealed The verse: “Whether you reveal what is in your souls or hide it, God will call you to account for it. Some of it has entered their hearts where nothing else had entered it.” The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “They said: We heard, we obeyed, and we submitted. So God placed faith in their hearts, and God Almighty revealed: The Messenger believed in what It was sent down to him from his Lord and the believers. God does not burden a soul except within its capacity. It is for it what it has earned and it is upon it what it has earned. Our Lord, do not hold us accountable if We forgot or made a mistake. He said: I have done so. Our Lord, do not place upon us a burden as You placed upon those before us. He said: I have done so. Our Lord, do not burden us with what we cannot bear, but pardon us and forgive us and have mercy on us. You are our Master, so help us against the disbelieving people. He said: “I have done so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10548","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Protest Adam and Moses, peace be upon them, and Moses said to him: O Adam, God created you with His hand, and breathed into you of His Spirit, then He said to you: Be, and you were. Then He commanded The angels prostrated to you, then he said: Dwell in Paradise, you and your wife, and eat from it freely wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree. Then you would be among the wrongdoers. He forbade you from a single tree, so you disobeyed your Lord. Then Adam, peace be upon him, said: O Moses, did you not know that God Almighty has decreed? On this before He created me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Adam performed Hajj, Moses, Adam performed Hajj, Moses, he performed Hajj. Adam, Moses"
"10549","From us Abdul Rahman bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Karim Al Jazari, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu said Ignorance: If I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying near the Kaaba, I would go to him until he stepped on his neck, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: “If he had done so, the angels would have taken him with their eyes, and if the Jews had wished for death, they would have died and seen their seats in the Fire, even if “Those who made the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, leave and returned, finding neither money nor family.”"
"10550","I am Al-Haytham bin Ayyub, narrated by Yahya bin Zakaria, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He swore an oath with which he would give up his wealth, and he met God while He was angry with him, and its confirmation is in the Book of God: Indeed, those who buy are for the covenant of God and their oaths. A small price. Those will have no share in the Hereafter.” Then Al-Ash’ath bin Qais came and said: What is Abu Abd al-Rahman telling you? So we said: Such and such, and he said: By God, it was revealed about me and about so-and-so with whom I had a dispute. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your witnesses or his oath.” I said: Then he swears. He said: “Whoever swears an oath by which he swears money while in it he is a lie, he will meet God, and He is upon him.” “angry.” And God Almighty revealed the verse"
"10551","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, I am Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim al-Batin, and Abd al-Malik bin Ayan, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Ibn Masoud said: “This verse was revealed: Indeed, those who buy the covenant of God and their oaths for a small price, until the end of the verse, Then nothing has abrogated it, so whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim by swearing an oath, is one of the people of this verse.”"
"10552","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us — my father narrated to us — from Salih, from Ibn Shihab — that 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah informed him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas said: \"Abu Sufyan ibn Harb informed me that he was in Sham with a group of Quraysh who had come as merchants during the truce that existed between the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and the disbelievers of Quraysh.\" Abu Sufyan said: \"We found the messenger of Caesar in a part of Sham, and he set out with me and my companions until we came to Iliya. We were brought before him, and there he was sitting in his royal court, wearing the crown, with the scholars of the Romans around him. He said to his interpreter: 'Ask them: which of them is closest in lineage to this man who claims to be a prophet?' Abu Sufyan said: 'I am the closest of them to him in lineage.' He said: 'What is the relationship between you and him?' I said: 'He is my cousin.' He said: 'And there was no man from the Banu 'Abd Manaf in the caravan that day other than me.' Caesar said: 'Bring him near to me.' Then he commanded regarding my companions, and they were placed behind me at my shoulders. Then he said to his interpreter: 'Say to his companions: I am going to ask this man about this one who claims to be a prophet. If he lies, then call him a liar.' Abu Sufyan said: 'By Allah, were it not for the shame that day that my companions would attribute a lie to me, I would have told him about him when he asked me. But I was too shy to have them attribute a lie to me, so I spoke truthfully about him.' Then he said to his interpreter: 'Say to him: how is this man's lineage among you?' I said: 'He is of good lineage among us.' He said: 'Has anyone among you said this saying before him?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Were you accusing him of lying before he said what he said?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Was there any king among his forefathers?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Did the noble people follow him, or their weak ones?' I said: 'Rather, their weak ones.' He said: 'Are they increasing or decreasing?' I said: 'Rather, they are increasing.' He said: 'Does anyone apostatize out of anger for his religion after having entered it?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Does he betray?' I said: 'No. And we are currently in a truce with him, and we fear that he might betray.' Abu Sufyan said: 'No word was possible for me to insert something by which I would diminish him, fearing that something other than it would be reported about me.' He said: 'Have you fought him, and has he fought you?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'How was your war and his war?' I said: 'It was alternating and shifting — sometimes the turn would be against us, and sometimes we would have the turn against him.' He said: 'What did he command you with?' I said: 'He commands us to worship Allah alone and not to associate anything with Him. He forbids us from what our forefathers used to worship. He commands us with prayer, truthfulness, chastity, fulfillment of the covenant, and rendering of the trust.'\" When I said that, he said to his interpreter: \"Say to him: I asked you about his lineage among you, and you claimed that he is of good lineage among you. And so the messengers are sent among the lineage of their people. I asked you: has anyone among you said this saying before him? And you claimed: no. I said: if anyone among you had said this saying before him, I would say: a man following a saying said before him. I asked you: were you accusing him of lying before he said what he said? And you claimed: no. And so I knew that it was not for him to leave lying upon the people and lie upon Allah. I asked you: was there any king among his forefathers? And you claimed: no. I said: if there had been a king among his forefathers, I would say: a man seeking the kingdom of his forefathers. I asked you: did the noble people follow him, or their weak ones? And you claimed that their weak ones followed him, and they are the followers of the messengers. I asked you: are they increasing or decreasing? And you claimed that they are increasing. And so it is with faith until it is complete. I asked you: does anyone apostatize out of anger for his religion after having entered it? And you claimed: no. And so it is with faith when it mingles with the joy of the heart — no one hates it. I asked you: does he betray? And you claimed: no. And so the messengers do not betray. I asked you: have you fought him and has he fought you? And you claimed that he has, and that your war and his war is alternating — sometimes the turn is against you, and sometimes you have the turn against him. And so it is with the messengers: they are tested, and for them is the ultimate outcome. I asked you: what did he command you with? And you claimed that he commands you to worship Allah alone and not to associate anything with Him, and forbids you from what your forefathers used to worship, and commands you with prayer, truthfulness, chastity, fulfillment of the covenant, and rendering of the trusts.' He said: 'This is the description of a prophet. I already knew that he would come forth, but I did not think he would be from you. And if what you have said is true, then it is near that he will possess the place of these two feet of mine. By Allah, if I hoped to reach him, I would undertake the effort to meet him. And if I were with him, I would wash from his feet.'\" Abu Sufyan said: \"Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and ordered that it was to be read. And in it was: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the great of the Romans. Peace be upon whoever follows the guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit, and you shall be safe. Submit, and Allah will give you your reward twice over. And if you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Arisiyyin. Say: O People of the Book, come to a word of equity between us and you — that we shall worship none but Allah, and shall not associate anything with Him, and shall not take one another as lords besides Allah. And if they turn away, then say: Bear witness that we are Muslims.'\" Abu Sufyan said: \"When he had finished his words, the voices of the Romans around him from among the great ones of the Romans rose, and their clamor increased. I do not know what they said. He commanded regarding us, and we were brought out.\" Abu Sufyan said: \"When I went out with my companions and was free with them, I said: 'The affair of Ibn Abi Kabsha has been commanded — this king of the Banu al-Asfar fears him.'\" Abu Sufyan said: \"By Allah, I remained in a state of humiliation, certain that his affair would become manifest, until Allah brought Islam into my heart while I was unwilling.\""
"10553","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “There was a man from Al-Ansar converted to Islam, then he apostatized and joined polytheism, then he regretted it and sent to his people: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: May I have some Repentance? Then his people came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: So-and-so has regretted it, and he has commanded us to ask you: Is it his right? Of repentance? Then it was revealed: How will God guide a people who disbelieved after their belief to One who is Forgiving and Merciful? So He sent to him, and he submitted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10554","Harun bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Ma'n, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Talha, he was the Ansari who had the most wealth in the city in terms of palm trees, and the most beloved of his wealth was Bayruha, which was facing the mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to enter it, eat of its fruit, and drink of water containing good things. Anas said: When it was revealed, This verse: You will not attain righteousness until you spend from what you love. Abu Talha went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger God, God says: You will not attain righteousness until you spend of what you love, and the most beloved of my wealth to me is relief, and it is charity for God, I hope Its righteousness and its treasure are with God, so put it, O Messenger of God, where God has shown you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Screw it, that is money.” Winner, and I heard what you said, and I think that you should give it to the closest ones.” Abu Talha said: “I will do it, O Messenger of God,” so Abu divided it. Talha among his relatives and cousins"
"10555","I am Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, narrated by Bahz, narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, narrated by Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “When it was revealed: You will not attain righteousness until you spend Of what you love. Abu Talha said: I see our Lord asking us for our wealth, so I call you as witness, O Messenger of God, that I have made my land for God. He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Put it on your relatives.” So he made it on Hassan bin Thabit and Ubayy bin Ka’b."
"10556","From his book, from Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, from his book, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, from Shu’bah, from Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He told him, when they were brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “What do you find in your book?” They said: We do not find stoning, so Abdullah said. Ibn Salam: They lied, stoning is in their book, so it was said: Then bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful. So they brought the Torah, and it came. Their reader, so he placed his palm on the place of stoning, and began to recite everything other than that. Abdullah bin Salam said: Insert your palm, and lo! stoning was indicated, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to be stoned, so they were stoned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10557","I am Bishr ibn Khalid, I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abraham speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He asked him about the first mosque built for the people. He said: “The Sacred Mosque and the Holy House.” He was asked: How much is the difference between them? ? He said: “For forty years, and wherever prayer takes you, pray, and then there is a mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10558","I am Bishr bin Khaled, I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “O you who have believed, fear Allah as He deserves to be feared, and do not die except as Muslims, as if a drop of Zaqqum were dropped on the earth.” It has imposed on the people of the earth their livelihood, so what about the one whose food is there, or who has no food other than it?"
"10559","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, from Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Maysarah, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “You are the best nation ever brought forth for mankind.” He said: “We are the best of people for mankind. We will bring them the shackles around their necks and bring them into Islam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10560","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, he is Amr, I am Israel, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of God Almighty: “You were the best nation brought forth for mankind.” He said: “They are the ones who migrated with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Medina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
